### 5. Feng et al. (2024 online / 2025 publication)

Application of Spectroscopic Technology with Machine Learning in Chinese Herbs from Seeds to Medicinal Materials: The Case of Genus Paris

Journal of Pharmaceutical Analysis, 2025, 15(2)

Research contributions

- Reviewed spectroscopy and machine learning for medicinal-herb quality assessment.
- Examined identification of germplasm, growth years, cultivars, and geographical origins.
- Discussed the application of UV-Vis, infrared, Raman, NMR, and other spectroscopic methods.
- Investigated quality monitoring from seeds through cultivation and processing.
- Proposed combining spectral information, machine learning, and blockchain to improve herbal traceability.

Research gaps

- Focuses on the genus Paris, limiting direct generalization to other medicinal plant species.
- Does not implement a complete blockchain-integrated spectroscopy and machine-learning system.
- Does not establish a unified database linking spectral fingerprints with blockchain batch records.
- Requires further validation of machine-learning models using larger, geographically diverse datasets.
- Does not demonstrate real-time automated authentication across all supply-chain stages.

