## 8\. Most important research gap to target

If you intend to develop a research paper or PhD research topic, I would prioritize the following gap:

Recommended research directionIntegration of AI/ML-based medicinal plant authentication and spectroscopy-based chemical quality verification with blockchain-enabled end-to-end traceability.

Why this direction is promising:

- The 2019 and 2025 reviews establish the need for better botanical traceability.
- The 2020 study introduces blockchain and IoT integration.
- The 2021 cannabis study highlights the limitation of relying solely on digital records for physical authenticity.
- The 2025 spectroscopy review identifies opportunities to combine machine learning, chemical analysis, and blockchain.
- The 2026 BioTrace platform advances Ayurvedic traceability but still leaves room for independently validated, automated physical and chemical authentication.

This creates a research opportunity beyond simply developing another blockchain traceability application.

One important consideration: BioTrace (2026) already proposes several features, including Hyperledger Fabric, IPFS, species verification, laboratory metrics, and QR verification. Therefore, claiming that blockchain + IPFS + QR codes alone is a novel contribution would be difficult to justify.

Your novelty should instead be demonstrated through an experimentally validated integration of botanical identification, chemical quality authentication, and trustworthy batch-level traceability.

